      "card_ids": ["C52","C56","C57","C58","C59","C60","C62","C63"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic-clearance/metabolic-stability records for close fluoroquinolone analogs do not indicate extensive first-pass loss: the aminopyrrolidine parent fluoroquinolone 2 has HLM CLint 33.49 µL/min/mg, HLM half-life 41 min, and enhanced microsomal/plasma stability (C66, C67, C69, C74); moxifloxacin has low hepatocyte CLint 3.01 µL/min/10^6 cells (C65); enrofloxacin has HLM half-life 43.1 min (C70). Trovafloxacin undergoes UGT acyl-glucuronidation (C64, C73), yet its oral F is 87.6–88%, so this pathway is not threshold-relevant negative evidence.",
      "card_ids": ["C64","C65","C66","C67","C69","C70","C73","C74"]
    }
