  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because the query is a fluoroquinolone with a C7 basic amine and N1 cyclopropyl-type substituent; direct L1/L2 F values for close analogs are all >=20% (moxifloxacin 86–97%, trovafloxacin 87.6–88%, levofloxacin/ofloxacin ~100%, norfloxacin mean 40%), and L3/L4 records support substantial oral exposure and near-complete absorption. L5 gut-wall efflux records show fluoroquinolones can be efflux substrates, but this mechanism does not reduce class F below 20% and moxifloxacin shows only weak efflux. L6 hepatic-clearance/metabolic-stability records for close analogs show moderate-to-low intrinsic clearance and enhanced microsomal stability, with no affirmative threshold-relevant evidence of F <20%; confidence remains moderate because the exact query transporter/first-pass profile is not directly measured."
}

